    <h1>Welcome to the home of Africa’s best-loved chicken brand</h1>
    <h2>Who is Hungry Lion?</h2>
    <p>Hungry Lion is a quick service restaurant built to bring joy to employees, customers and local communities through food, served with passion. It started as a small eatery in 1997. The same focus on taste and generous portions turned it into a household name in South Africa, Zambia, Namibia, Botswana, Eswatini, Lesotho, Angola, Zimbabwe and Mauritius.</p>
    <h2>Our story</h2>
    <p>The first restaurant opened in 1997 in Eikestad Mall, Stellenbosch. Four more stores followed that year, including two in Zambia and one in the Eastern Cape. Namibia came in 1998. Eswatini and Botswana followed in 1999, Angola in 2010, Lesotho in 2024, and Zimbabwe and Mauritius in 2025. In 2025 Hungry Lion opened its 500th store and passed 10,000 employees.</p>
    <h2>Our food</h2>
    <p>The menu is fried chicken, wings, burgers, chips, drinks and ice cream, with regular specials. Pieces are fried fresh and the chips are thick-cut. The Namibia menu and prices are on this site.</p>
    <h2>Our commitment</h2>
    <p>Stores grow their own managers. Training and promotion from inside the restaurants is how the network expands, and new stores mean more local jobs. Hungry Lion does not offer franchise opportunities.</p>
